   -=-=-Storyline-=-=-
	You are about to enter the world of The Dragon's Lair. Things here are
like things in other lands, with slight exceptions. Here, warriors constantly
train and better themselves for the harshness the land causes...
	The King of your town, Matriar, is a rude, and mean one. Due to his
own set of beliefs, he renders all magic "evil", save healing potions, which
saved his life some time back. No magic using citizens occupy this town, save
a few clerics that live with the guards, and in the arena.
	There is a vast forest outside of town, a huge set of mountains, a
deep dungeon a few miles away, a vast ocean, and if you can find the owner of
the airship, you have all the world to explore. All these come as you get
stronger in levels.

     -=-=-Instructions/User Input-=-=-
	o Generally, whenever you see a red line, it will be a command prompt.
	  This is a point where you are required to type something, and give
	  the game whatever information it is asking for.
	o When entering in numbers for anything (weapon number, GP Withdrawl,
	  etc.) do not enter anything abnormal. I.e. something like "10-" will
	  give you an error, and you _will_ lose your turn. You can enter
	  comas, however, to help you out when entering numbers.
	o Most of the time, information will be given in the following format:
	  - Light Blue colors will usually indicate a type of something.
	  - Bright Blue colors will usually indicate the actual value of the
	    type.
	  - Green colors are usually info of some sort.
	  - White is used as the input from user, along with certain points
	    to make certain _important_ info stand out.
	  - Red is usually used from command prompts, where the game is
	    expecting input from you.
	  - Bright Green colors are usually a type of command you are supposed
	    to enter.
	  - Texts inside of () inside of a command prompt, are usually either
	    a maximum amount of something, in which case a max= will be
	    displayed before a number, or just a number. In the latter case,
	    the number will be the default for when "RETURN" is pressed.
	  - Command prompts that look similar to this: "Run? ([Y]/N) " Yes
	    also have a default for return. Whenever a prompt like this pops
	    ups, it generally has a default. (If neither of the options is
	    enclosed by a [] then there is no default) Otherwise, whichever
	    command is inside of the [] is the default when a "RETURN" or
	    any other key is pressed other than the one _not_ inside the [].

     -=-=-Instructions/Stats-=-=-
	o Name:		 This is obvious. This is your character's name.
	o Class:	 Your class is a profession. The Fighter is all that
			 is available at this time.
	o HitPoints:	 This is your current life power. The higher the
			 better. When this number hits 0 or below, you will
			 die. Try your hardest not to let this happen to live
			 longer.
	o Max HitPoints: This is your maximum hitpoints.
	o Experience:	 This is how experienced you are in your class. This
			 number rises with battles, boxing, etc. This number
			 reflects your level.
	o Level-Up Need: This is how much experience you need to advance to
			 the next level.
	o Level:	 This number reflects your ability in your class. The
			 higher the better. The current range is 1-21. At 21st
			 level, you will go on a quest on honor.
	o Strength:	 This number reflects your brute power. The higher the
			 number, the more damaging your attacks will be. This
			 number also reflects how frequently you will hit.
	o Dexterity:	 This number reflects your speed, and agility. The
			 higher your dexterity, the lower your Armor Class.
			 This number also reflects on running away, and other
			 miscellaneous encounters.
	o Intelligence:	 This number reflects how smart you are.
	o Wisdom:	 This number reflects how "street" smart you are, or
			 how in touch you are with psychic abilities.
	o Constitution:	 This number reflects your life-force. The higher this
			 number, the higher your hitpoints will be at a
			 level-up. This number also reflects checks against
			 diseases, poison, etc.
	o Gold Pieces:	 This is the currency in this land. Everything is
			 charged in gold pieces.
	o In Bank:	 This number reflects how many gold pieces you
			 currently have in the bank.
	o Armor Class:	 This number reflects how powerful your defense is.
			 This number combines your dexterity bonus, plus your
			 armor and shield defense. The lower this number is
			 the better your defense is. (i.e. 10 is the worst,
			 while -99 is the best...)
	o Joust Points:	 This number reflects your skill in jousting. The
			 higher this number, the better of a jouster you are.
	o Boxing Level:	 This number reflects the level of skill you have in
			 boxing. The higher the better. The at __% is the
			 percent of completion you have of the next level.
			 When this number reaches 100% or greater, you will
			 advance a level.
	o Boxing Points: This number reflects your skill in boxing. The higher
			 the better.
	o Total Turns:	 This number is the total number of times you have
			 played "The Dragon's Lair".
	o Turns Left:	 This number reflects how many turns you have
			 remaining for today.

     -=-=-Instructions/Equipment-=-=-
	o Left Hand:		    This is what is in your Left Hand. This
				    is also the default weapon when another
				    user attacks you, so it is important to
				    have your primary weapon in this hand.
	o Right Hand:		    This is what is in your Right Hand. This
				    is where you must hold a shield, if you
				    choose to use one, but you may also have
				    a secondary weapon in this hand as well.
	o Left Finger:		    This is the ring that is on your Left
				    Finger, if any.
	o Right Finger:		    This is the ring that is on your Right
				    Finger, if any.
	o Body:			    This is what is around your body.
				    Generally, this is armor.
	o Head:			    This is what is on your head. Generally
				    this is a helmet of some sort.
	o Hands:		    This is what goes over your hands. Usually
				    these are gloves.
	o Waist:		    This is what is around your waist. Usually
				    will be a pouch of some sort that will be
				    attached to your belt.
	o Belt:			    This is whatever belt you are wearing.
	o Brooch:		    This is whatever brooch you have on you.
				    (Note: A brooch is an ornamental pin,
				    button, or buckle, used as a memento, a
				    charm, or simply a fastener for a certain
				    type of clothing.)
	o Feet:			    This is whatever is on your feet. Usually
				    boots of some sort.
	o Wrists:		    This is what is around your wrist. This
				    will usually be bracers of a sort.
	o Necklace:		    This is what necklace you have around your
				    neck.
	o Pendant:		    This is what type of pendant, if any, you
				    have attached to your necklace.
	o Item #1-#5:		    These are slots for any other
			            miscellaneous objects.
	o Potions Of Healing:	    These are magical potions that restore 4
				    to 10 lost hitpoints. Your healed
				    hitpoints will never go above your maximum
				    hitpoints.
	o Potions Of Extra-Healing: These are more powerful magical potions
				    that restore 6 to 27 lost hitpoints. Your
				    healed hitpoints will never go above your
				    maximum hitpoints.

     -=-=-Tips & Hints-=-=-
	o At level 4 you can enter the forest, level 9 the mountains, 14 the
	  ocean, at level 18 the dungeon, and at 20th the airship awaits.
	o Feel free to kill as many people, as many times as you can. It
	  never hurts to better yourself in a world as harsh as this.
	o To ressurect a player, it costs 50GP times that person's level.
	o Joust as many times as you can for extra GP.
	o Boxing other users will get your XP rewards.
	o The barkeep contains some valuable information...
	o The guards in the guardhouse also contain some top-secret
	  information.
	o At 21st level, you must go on a journey of faith...
	o Watch out for the guards, they love to execute people.
	o The most expensive weapon or armor is not neccissarily the best...
	  Experiment with weapons and armor to find the best...
	o For custom attack sentences, and battle cries, edit them in the
	  other options in the Arena.
	o Talk to other players through the spray wall located in the alley.
	o Chat with all players in the conversation hall in the arena!
	o Visit the jail to kill in-mates and recieve large XP and GP rewards!
	o In the forest, you can use your arrow or keypad to use movement,
	  other than typing in N,S,E, or W. (i.e. 8=N, 6=E, etc.)


